================================================================================
SOURCE
================================================================================
This is a fork of the official Zopfli compressor maintained by
Mr_KrzYch00. The original Google repository (https://github.com/google/zopfli)
has been archived since 2023; the KrzYmod fork continues to receive
updates and bug fixes. We use the MrKrzYch00 fork in preference to the
archived upstream so that we benefit from ongoing improvements.

================================================================================
WHAT WE USE
================================================================================
The library portion of the KrzYmod fork only. The following files are
copied verbatim from upstream master:

  adler.c/.h            blocksplitter.c/.h   crc32.c/.h
  defines.h              deflate.c/.h         gzip_container.c/.h
  hash.c/.h              katajainen.c/.h      lz77.c/.h
  squeeze.c/.h           tree.c/.h            util.c/.h
  zlib_container.c/.h    zopfli.h             zopfli_lib.c

The following KrzYmod-specific files are NOT included in zpaq-std:

  cache.c/.h            - zopfliDB stats cache (not needed for our use)
  inthandler.c/.h       - SIGINT handler for the CLI binary
  zip_container.c/.h    - ZIP container output (we only use deflate/zlib)
  zopfli_bin.c/.h       - the standalone zopfli CLI binary
  affinity.h            - macOS thread affinity (no-op on Linux/BSD)

================================================================================
API DIFFERENCES VS ORIGINAL GOOGLE/ZOPFLI
================================================================================
The KrzYmod fork adds 2 new parameters to ZopfliCompress():

  size_t ZopfliCompress(ZopfliOptions* options, ZopfliFormat output_type,
                        const unsigned char* in, size_t insize,
                        unsigned char** out, size_t* outsize,
                        ZopfliPredefinedSplits* sp,
                        const ZopfliAdditionalData* moredata);

The two new parameters (sp, moredata) are both nullable. Our wrapper
passes NULL for both, giving identical behavior to the original
google/zopfli API. ZopfliOptions has additional fields; we call
ZopfliInitOptions() to populate them with safe defaults.

